{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits","id":551458,"title":"Tiers and Traits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T07:51:41-07:00","id":551458,"title":"Tiers and Traits","content":"The second teaser is out.<br /> <br /> And I don't think I'm terribly thrilled, myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;Tier______________Practical Maximum&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;____________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;Potential Maximum&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93; &#91;COLOR=#FF0000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;Mundane&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;__________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;4&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;____________________________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;5&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93; &#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;Daredevil/Psion&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;_____&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;5&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;____________________________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;6&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93; &#91;COLOR=#FF0000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;Hero&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;/Proxy&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;_________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;5&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;____________________________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;6&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93; &#91;COLOR=#FF0000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;Demigod&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;/Nova&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;______&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;6&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;____________________________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;6&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93; &#91;COLOR=#FF0000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;God&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;/Terat&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;__________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;6&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;&#91;B&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;____________________________&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/B&#93;&#91;COLOR=#000000&#93;&#91;FONT=Times New Roman&#93;&#91;SIZE=16px&#93;7&#91;/SIZE&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;/COLOR&#93;</pre> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">I still need to see how the tiers work in action, but it looks like (without specialties and edges/merits/flaws) that effective difference in dice pools can only be three in difference. That sort of looks like they decided that anybody can be challenged by anyone. I call Grandma with a Shotgun against Atlas on the front lawn.<br /> <br /> The other thing is that they %#^%^!*(&amp; decided to rename every stat and make them NuWOD. So every Attribute is Force, Control or Resistance for your Physical, Mental or Social interactions.<br /> <br /> DAMMIT! </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 06-18-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:30:21-07:00","id":551564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">That sort of looks like they decided that anybody can be challenged by anyone. I call Grandma with a Shotgun against Atlas on the front lawn.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna respond with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arachne\" target=\"_blank\">Arachne and Athena on the loom</a>, so two out of three ain't bad. My requirements were a system where gods and mortals could meaningfully challenge each other, except when they don't. You're seeing the part of the system where they can meaningfully challenge each other. There's a Scale system that's referenced, but which you admittedly haven't seen.<br /> <br /> With different Scale permissions, even a higher-tier action doesn't have to benefit from Enhancements and the successes going further. This lets gods be subtly better than mortals, but really crank it out when they have Scale, which means their success go further than a mortal's.<br /> <br /> See also rishis slapping around Hindu gods, various demigods slapping around gods in their own pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 06-12-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:23:47-07:00","id":551672,"title":"","content":"To start, size for emphasis does not work when the majority of text is large. It just makes me surprised when I see normal text again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits#post551458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still need to see how the tiers work in action, but it looks like (without specialties and edges/merits/flaws) that effective difference in dice pools can only be three in difference. That sort of looks like they decided that anybody can be challenged by anyone. I call Grandma with a Shotgun against Atlas on the front lawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I like this change, as 'anybody who isn't sufficiently awesome cannot think of challenging me' was the major problem with Epic Attributes in 1e. I like that in 2e a god cannot just stomp on a master swordsmen, it makes those followers and creatures more relevant.<br /> <br /> For fun, let's compare granny with a shotgun to Athena:<br /> -Granny has 2 dots in finesse, and since most people don't use firearms on a regular basis probably 0 dots in marksmanship, maybe 1 or 2 if she lives in the countryside and has to deal with foxes trying to eat her chickens, so 2-4 dice and has a TN of 8.<br /> -Athena is probably a master at swordplay, and so has 5 dots in her weaponry skill plus 4-6 dots in Might/Finesse, depending on which is required fo hit. In addition, as a god she probably has a TN of 6 or 7. That's over twice GwaS's successes before applying other god bonuses. Athena is also likely set up to act first rather than GwaS.<br /> <br /> Also, imagine Bob the Scientist and Knowsalot, demigod of knowledge racing to discover cancer. Unless he's a world class expert in his field Bob probably only has 3 Reason and 3 Science, with other knowledge skills at 1 or 2. In contrast Knowsalot probably has 4-6 in Reason, and 3-5 in a lot of knowledge skills, giving him a greater base of knowledge to draw on. In addition, Knowsalot can probably do basic fate manipulation to just happen to run across important information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other thing is that they %#^%^!*(&amp; decided to rename every stat and make them NuWOD. So every Attribute is Force, Control or Resistance for your Physical, Mental or Social interactions.<br /> <br /> DAMMIT! </div> </div> </div>Eh, I actually like the new spread, especially mental attributes. It's one of the few places nWoD did well, standardising attributes.<br /> <br /> ...I'm now going to go and build Granny with a Shotgun, 60 year old scion of Ares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:33:25-07:00","id":551704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551672#post551672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm now going to go and build Granny with a Shotgun, 60 year old scion of Ares.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had no idea I wanted this until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:50:49-07:00","id":551838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551564#post551564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna respond with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arachne\" target=\"_blank\">Arachne and Athena on the loom</a>, so two out of three ain't bad. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">My requirements were a system where gods and mortals could meaningfully challenge each other, except when they don't.</span> You're seeing the part of the system where they can meaningfully challenge each other. There's a Scale system that's referenced, but which you admittedly haven't seen.<br /> <br /> With different Scale permissions, even a higher-tier action doesn't have to benefit from Enhancements and the successes going further. This lets gods be subtly better than mortals, but really crank it out when they have Scale, which means their success go further than a mortal's.<br /> <br /> See also rishis slapping around Hindu gods, various demigods slapping around gods in their own pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Capricious rules systems don't really make you feel epic. While Arachne vs. Athena is a valid 'challenge' there are still things like Feats of Strength such as Hercule lifting the world that are far more at the top end of 'superhuman'.<br /> <br /> (Heck, even with Arachne, I suspect that they both made nearly perfect tapestries with the materials provided, Arachne just had hubris for her subject matter. There's only so good you can make it due to materials, IMO.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551672#post551672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To start, size for emphasis does not work when the majority of text is large. It just makes me surprised when I see normal text again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't do any size change, I just tried to make the chart work correctly. Which this board software failed epically at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551672#post551672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First off, I like this change, as 'anybody who isn't sufficiently awesome cannot think of challenging me' was the major problem with Epic Attributes in 1e. I like that in 2e a god cannot just stomp on a master swordsmen, it makes those followers and creatures more relevant.<br /> <br /> For fun, let's compare granny with a shotgun to Athena:<br /> -Granny has 2 dots in finesse, and since most people don't use firearms on a regular basis probably 0 dots in marksmanship, maybe 1 or 2 if she lives in the countryside and has to deal with foxes trying to eat her chickens, so 2-4 dice and has a TN of 8.<br /> -Athena is probably a master at swordplay, and so has 5 dots in her weaponry skill plus 4-6 dots in Might/Finesse, depending on which is required fo hit. In addition, as a god she probably has a TN of 6 or 7. That's over twice GwaS's successes before applying other god bonuses. Athena is also likely set up to act first rather than GwaS.<br /> <br /> Also, imagine Bob the Scientist and Knowsalot, demigod of knowledge racing to discover cancer. Unless he's a world class expert in his field Bob probably only has 3 Reason and 3 Science, with other knowledge skills at 1 or 2. In contrast Knowsalot probably has 4-6 in Reason, and 3-5 in a lot of knowledge skills, giving him a greater base of knowledge to draw on. In addition, Knowsalot can probably do basic fate manipulation to just happen to run across important information.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference of too much scale (Scion 1E) and what we have here, which is essentially Tiers appear to be SFX effects to your Attributes. I get the feeling they may have gone too far the other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551672#post551672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I actually like the new spread, especially mental attributes. It's one of the few places nWoD did well, standardising attributes.<br /> <br /> ...I'm now going to go and build Granny with a Shotgun, 60 year old scion of Ares.</div> </div> </div> </div>I detest NuWOD stats, because it removes appearance as an attribute. (They also borked up the backgrounds of the supernaturals enough that I have yet to this day even bought one book of NuWOD). It's forcing elegance over fun. Some of us like being able to go &quot;Wow, damn are the guys on our team supermodels! How is that fair?&quot;<br /> <br /> Now it's &quot;Okay, Social effort. I'm rolling my Force against your Resistance. Don't give a flying @%@!&amp;* what the stats are, it's just dice rolls now.&quot;<br /> <br /> And you do realize I was referring to the fact that a mortal grandma looks to be able to actually affect Atlas, not a high tier demigod?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 06-12-2015, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:21:12-07:00","id":551866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551838#post551838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference of too much scale (Scion 1E) and what we have here, which is essentially Tiers appear to be SFX effects to your Attributes. I get the feeling they may have gone too far the other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point it's YMMV, we need to wait until we get the scaling system in full.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I detest NuWOD stats, because it removes appearance as an attribute. (They also borked up the backgrounds of the supernaturals enough that I have yet to this day even bought one book of NuWOD). It's forcing elegance over fun. Some of us like being able to go &quot;Wow, damn are the guys on are team super-models! How is that fair?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Appearance is weird. It's not of much use if it just measures how hot you are (which caries considerably with the beholder), and is extremely useful if it's how you use your looks. I'd love your social stats to be Presence (force of personality), Appearance (ability to use your looks), and Composure (ability to remain calm), but I'll settle for others. Also, Striking Looks 1 is model attractive, while 2 is drop dead gorgeous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now it's &quot;Okay, Social effort. I'm rolling my Force against your Control. Don't give a flying @%@!&amp;* what the stats are, it's just dice rolls now.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It was 'just dice rolls' before. I'd prefer it if the 'physical force, mental force, etc.' was left out of the sheet and 90% of the rules, but it's not that much different from how Shadowrun sets up it's stats (physical and mental of: power, speed, finesse, and resilience).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you do realize I was referring to the fact that a mortal grandma looks to be able to actually affect Atlas, not a high tier demigod? </div> </div> </div>Okay, I don't actually know which atlas we're talking about here. <span style=\"color:blue\">If this is the book then I'm ashamed it doesn't have the ability to roll and drop itself on GwaS's foot</span>. If it's any other, can I please get his abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 06-12-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:21:52-07:00","id":551867,"title":"","content":"Trying to judge the differences between the Tiers with just this is a bit impossible from everything the devs have said. Even then, you're not really being fair to how even these base mechanics impact conflicts between Tiers.<br /> <br /> We know the TN changes with Tier. Anyone experienced with the cWOD can tell you how major this is. A character rolling against a TN of 8 vs. a TN of 6 is at a massive disadvantage. Consider for a moment that 6 dice at TN 6 is better than 10 dice at TN 8 with the mechanics we know about so far without taking into account all the other widgets and dials in the game. A maxed out mundane needs more than dice if they want to go up against a higher tier PC that's only a bit above average in the same area.<br /> <br /> So without any of the many, many other things that could impact a contest between two characters, high tiers have massive advantages even without major differences in dice. In my mind, that's a good thing. Having to have massive dice pools, or manage huge numbers of extra successes to differential tiers was extremely clunky in comparison.<br /> <br /> The fact that Granny might be able to hit Atlas also doesn't mean she can actually effect Atlas. This isn't the nWOD where successful attack rolls with a shotgun mean a minimum of 4L damage. Granny still had to do with with the Difficulty of the roll, any Complications, and putting what Effects she manages to have after that into play.<br /> <br /> Tiers are SFX on the basic dice mechanics and Attributes. They're also going to be a lot more. Remember we're being teased with a core system that Scion will be one game line built off of, not the new Scion system in full. Even with the Sardonyx core system fully spoiler where we get to see things like Scale, Intensity, and the new combat systems, we still aren't looking at the specifics that Scion uses.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Can we also not push for some sort of weird quasi-edition war regarding the nWOD? If you want to discuss the pros and cons of the Sardonyx Attribute spreads, lets do that. Not just bash the nWOD and claim that's a critique of what Sardonyx is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:33:21-07:00","id":552004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551866#post551866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I don't actually know which atlas we're talking about here. <span style=\"color:blue\">If this is the book then I'm ashamed it doesn't have the ability to roll and drop itself on GwaS's foot</span>. If it's any other, can I please get his abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlas_%28mythology%29\" target=\"_blank\">The Titan Atlas.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:12:18-07:00","id":552058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551867#post551867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know the TN changes with Tier. Anyone experienced with the cWOD can tell you how major this is. A character rolling against a TN of 8 vs. a TN of 6 is at a massive disadvantage. Consider for a moment that 6 dice at TN 6 is better than 10 dice at TN 8 with the mechanics we know about so far without taking into account all the other widgets and dials in the game. A maxed out mundane needs more than dice if they want to go up against a higher tier PC that's only a bit above average in the same area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're going to go with changing target dice numbers. Changing target numbers on the dice is bad game design, and there's a good reason almost every game system has moved away from the practice. It slows down gameplay, confuses players, and messes with dice scripts. I think they're referencing how the result of your successes will be different depending on your tier.<br /> <br /> For example, a Hero gets 5 successes an throws a car. A Demigod gets 5 successes and throws a building. A God gets 5 successes and throws a large mountain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:24:23-07:00","id":552077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552058#post552058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they're going to go with changing target dice numbers. Changing target numbers on the dice is bad game design, and there's a good reason almost every game system has moved away from the practice. It slows down gameplay, confuses players, and messes with dice scripts. I think they're referencing how the result of your successes will be different depending on your tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we're changing target numbers (and also referencing how the result of your successes are different depending on Tier).<br /> <br /> There's good reason everyone's moved away from changing it on the fly (it alters dice probabilities too much to adjudicate wisely, messes with success counting, and requires a decent eyeball) but this isn't on the fly - they're static depending on Tier, which remains (relatively) constant in play. It worked well in Exalted and Mummy, and it works fine here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 06-12-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:56:35-07:00","id":552117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits#post551458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second teaser is out.<br /> <br /> And I don't think I'm terribly thrilled, myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> The other thing is that they %#^%^!*(&amp; decided to rename every stat and make them NuWOD. So every Attribute is Force, Control or Resistance for your Physical, Mental or Social interactions.<br /> <br /> DAMMIT!</div> </div> </div> </div>I AM thrilled, however. Well, not exactly thrilled, as the concept of God level succes applying differently than human's is a little bit... weird,and i think i'll need to see how does that actually works before judging it. BUT. That attribute change? Thank you. Thank you SO much. That was one of the changes i asked for, and i'm thrilled about that.<br /> <br /> Thank you because now i can create a God that simply refuses some other because he's goddamn iron-willed when the full Manipulation smartass God comes knocking and saying &quot;ey, sorry about all your concept (brutish but utterly determined to a goal) buuuuut 10 Manipulation, Suck my...&quot; <br /> <br /> And why Appearance is needed as an Atribute anyway. NWoD has Striking Looks, asTwoDSix said. And i'm failry sure the devs have in mind that Afrodite, and that merit in special receives bonus, or Tier applications, or what not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:01:27-07:00","id":552124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551867#post551867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Granny might be able to hit Atlas also doesn't mean she can actually effect Atlas. This isn't the nWOD where successful attack rolls with a shotgun mean a minimum of 4L damage. Granny still had to do with with the Difficulty of the roll, any Complications, and putting what Effects she manages to have after that into play.<br /> <br /> Tiers are SFX on the basic dice mechanics and Attributes. They're also going to be a lot more. Remember we're being teased with a core system that Scion will be one game line built off of, not the new Scion system in full. Even with the Sardonyx core system fully spoiler where we get to see things like Scale, Intensity, and the new combat systems, we still aren't looking at the specifics that Scion uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we do not know that a mortal mob might be able to kill a god or not. But right now, it's looking a little too feasible.<br /> <br /> It sounds like the Epic just got its feet kicked out from under it. Especially when you tack in modern weapons and explosives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:20:33-07:00","id":552171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552124#post552124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we do not know that a mortal mob might be able to kill a god or not. But right now, it's looking a little too feasible.<br /> <br /> It sounds like the Epic just got its feet kicked out from under it. Especially when you tack in modern weapons and explosives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Demigod McScion, and possibly even Hero McScion, can use so much better than a mortal. And God McScion is even better at it.<br /> <br /> And where is this mob getting all these modern weapons? Where I live it's unlikely that they have shotgun liscenes, and anything else is going to be criminal underworld or military only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=551704#post551704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I had no idea I wanted this until now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to offer suggestions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0