/> Self Healing<br /> Solipsistic Well-being<br /> Rabbit Reflexes<br /> <br /> <u>Virtues</u><br /> Expression 3<br /> Intellect 1<br /> Valor 4<br /> Vengeance 1<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> 4<br /> <b>Legend Points:</b> 16<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> 0x6, incapacitated<br /> Dodge DV: 10<br /> Parry DV: 9<br /> Join Battle: 7<br /> Soak: 7(10)B, 5(7)L, 3(5)A<br /> <br /> Lawn Defender:<br /> Acc 9(+4), DMG 8L, Speed 4, Range 20</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 06-12-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:52:29-07:00","id":552196,"title":"","content":"What's a shotgun license? Though, any mob that's using a gun in a mob setting is 1) doing it wrong and 2) gonna get more of them than the godling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:41:25-07:00","id":552281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552124#post552124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we do not know that a mortal mob might be able to kill a god or not. But right now, it's looking a little too feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what?<br /> <br /> All we know right now from the documents is that a mundane with a decent dice pool can be a challenge for a high tier entity that is using <b>none</b> of their powers/abilities.<br /> <br /> Which isn't actually any different from Scion 1e. Ignoring the mechanical stupidity of this, if I make a Scion Demigod with no direct combat powers (including no physical Epics), and go up against the worlds best skilled mortal fighter, and I don't use any of the social/mental powers I did buy up like mad instead of combat stuff, or any of those innate things I can do with Legend, then it isn't a surefire win. If I go up against a mob under the same conditions, it is again not a sure thing.<br /> <br /> That's what you're effectively judging on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounds like the Epic just got its feet kicked out from under it. Especially when you tack in modern weapons and explosives. </div> </div> </div>Based on... what exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:06:42-07:00","id":552521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552124#post552124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like the Epic just got its feet kicked out from under it. Especially when you tack in modern weapons and explosives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tanks and grenades ain't worth shit if you're going up against Lord Shiva's Teen Baan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:58:10-07:00","id":552622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552077#post552077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's good reason everyone's moved away from changing it on the fly (it alters dice probabilities too much to adjudicate wisely, messes with success counting, and requires a decent eyeball) but this isn't on the fly - they're static depending on Tier, which remains (relatively) constant in play. It worked well in Exalted and Mummy, and it works fine here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was one of the things that players always moaned about at my table whenever we played Exalted, so we stayed away from Sidereals for exactly those reasons. But as long as the target numbers are static throughout an entire tier it should be stable enough that players will get used to it. It will require adjusting dice scripts every tier (for those that prefer to use phone Apps, or other dice rolling aids) but that is infrequent enough that it just might work. I'm definitely willing to give it a try!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:57:40-07:00","id":553233,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as long as you're a Hero tier, you have the same target number. That's a fairly long career with a single TN in play. It's not changing from roll to roll or scene to scene.<br /> <br /> When you graduate to Demigod tier, it's like a little reward. &quot;Forget your old TN, because you're better than that now.&quot; It's more of a momentous occasion than anything else, and odds are that the new TN will never go back down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:36:54-07:00","id":556215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits#post551458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I call Grandma with a Shotgun against Atlas on the front lawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assault rifle counts?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://youngfilmreaders.files.wordpress.com/2013/02/article-1298854-0a891e1a000005dc-1000_468x286.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> If so, check. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:31:14-07:00","id":557119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552171#post552171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where is this mob getting all these modern weapons? Where I live it's unlikely that they have shotgun liscenes, and anything else is going to be criminal underworld or military only.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you don' t live in the US then. In the US, there is no lisence needed for a shotgun or a hunting rifle. You can buy them at Walmart... Just about every household in my hometown as at least one shotgun or rifle in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:47:12-07:00","id":557142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=552622#post552622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was one of the things that players always moaned about at my table whenever we played Exalted, so we stayed away from Sidereals for exactly those reasons. But as long as the target numbers are static throughout an entire tier it should be stable enough that players will get used to it. It will require adjusting dice scripts every tier (for those that prefer to use phone Apps, or other dice rolling aids) but that is infrequent enough that it just might work. I'm definitely willing to give it a try!</div> </div> </div> </div>Time to lurk no more. As someone who plays primarily system utilizing similar type of tiered target number I feel I can add to discussion. It works. It feels very smooth and, while you do feel yourself stronger. it is not automatically overpowering and you are not suddenly that much better,than others by just jumping tier. Players do not tend to have problems remembering it(outside of the time immediately after the switch)<br /> It will be interesting, what other goodies will accompany this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T14:32:01-07:00","id":557342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=557119#post557119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you don' t live in the US then. In the US, there is no lisence needed for a shotgun or a hunting rifle. You can buy them at Walmart... Just about every household in my hometown as at least one shotgun or rifle in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I live in the UK, where we actually have vaguely sane gun laws. I've met one person in my life who is used to guns, because she comes from a farming village in Wales, and I know nobody who owns a gun.<br /> <br /> Oh, and combat systems assuming guns are easily available is a pet peeve of mine (I've had PCs on the run for being seen with a collection of rifles). I get good chuncks of the combat and gear chapter being completely useless, as everybody avoids taking guns unless told it is that type of game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:41:42-07:00","id":558301,"title":"","content":"I get that, but when a large portion of the fanbase lives in the US, they kinda have to include all the guns and stuff. I know if I was going out to a fight (especially a serious myth powered one) I'd bring my bedside pistol with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:11:54-07:00","id":558322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=558301#post558301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, but when a large portion of the fanbase lives in the US, they kinda have to include all the guns and stuff. I know if I was going out to a fight (especially a serious myth powered one) I'd bring my bedside pistol with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e Scion is brilliant about this, if I remember correctly the rules for guns take up a fraction of a page, with another half a page for different gun types, and this doesn't change in the entire run. Nowhere near as bad as 2e Vampire: the Masquerade, which provided in the player's guide a 2 page table to guns where there were several instances per category of guns being EXACTLY the same. What bugs me is if they then skimp on things like grappling, hitting with the back of the blade/pommel strikes, and other combat techniques I might actually use and can be described in a few paragraphs, in favour of giving more focus to guns. But again, in 1e Scion the gun rules are pretty much 'as other ranged weapons, but with a couple of minor changes'.<br /> <br /> And I know that if I was going out to participate in a serious myth powered fight, I'd care about having people with me (followers), then grabbing a shield before carrying a gun. They start to lose their effectiveness against the bigger stuff (and I mean size-wise). A decent sword is as good a bet (especially against giants or dragons), especially as I don't trust myself to be able to aim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T22:19:39-07:00","id":559073,"title":"","content":"Unless you use some house rules for Followers and Companions, they basically became totally irrelevant by about Legend 6. Scion 1E had no way of balancing your Mentor 5 at Hero (an Amazon, IIRC) versus the Mentor 5 at God (Imhotep, Legend 12 God). That just... 'happened', without an explanation for how you traded up your mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T02:19:34-07:00","id":559162,"title":"","content":"Guide 5 was always a god. And yeah, I always thought that followers should become more for the dot at certain points of legend (e.g. at Demigod level all followers drop one dot in cost, and again at god tlevel), and creatures should mature with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:34:20-07:00","id":559305,"title":"","content":"So Teaser #3 is out.<br /> <br /> The first thing I get out of initiative is that you can't be good at anything, unless you have a large dice pool in everything. That's kind of pushing things toward 'everyone is mediocre' level, especially with comments (from RPG.net readers) about different combat actions requiring random dice pools.<br /> <br /> I especially hate that when you have focus (ie. you are taking an action) there is no 'just fail', you will botch. That's making it a damn system of failure, not success. Like back when 1s used to subtract from any successes and you didn't succeed unless you rolled more successes than 1s.<br /> <br /> Looking back on Tiers, I think the thing I hate about how it is currently set up is that it tends to give a median maximum that is higher (by the difficulty target being easier) but that if you have a bout of bad luck, a lower tier can actually do just as good. The best either of them can do is all 10s, but that's only a difference in the maximum success of maybe 2 successes.<br /> <br /> It's only a tendency to do better, but you can't actually have a truly 'greater' success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:07:03-07:00","id":559499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=559305#post559305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Teaser #3 is out.<br /> <br /> The first thing I get out of initiative is that you can't be good at anything, unless you have a large dice pool in everything. That's kind of pushing things toward 'everyone is mediocre' level, especially with comments (from RPG.net readers) about different combat actions requiring random dice pools.<br /> <br /> I especially hate that when you have focus (ie. you are taking an action) there is no 'just fail', you will botch. That's making it a damn system of failure, not success. Like back when 1s used to subtract from any successes and you didn't succeed unless you rolled more successes than 1s.<br /> <br /> Looking back on Tiers, I think the thing I hate about how it is currently set up is that it tends to give a median maximum that is higher (by the difficulty target being easier) but that if you have a bout of bad luck, a lower tier can actually do just as good. The best either of them can do is all 10s, but that's only a difference in the maximum success of maybe 2 successes.<br /> <br /> It's only a tendency to do better, but you can't actually have a truly 'greater' success.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on these issues<br /> 1. My math fu is weak and thus I cannot comment.<br /> <br /> 2.Yeah, I hope Focus as written dies in fire, but I think it is here to generate momentum for future use, so you can then succeed more, still crappy mechanic though and I do think this will get rework.<br /> <br /> 3. I think this is where Scale comes in, so higher tier will always have greater success, if they succeed, which they do easily , as long as it is Scaled &quot;ability&quot; versus Scaled &quot;ability&quot;, and those without Scaled powers need not to apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:01:44-07:00","id":560051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/551458-tiers-and-traits?p=559499#post559499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I think this is where Scale comes in, so higher tier will always have greater success, if they succeed, which they do easily , as long as it is Scaled &quot;ability&quot; versus Scaled &quot;ability&quot;, and those without Scaled powers need not to apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that scale only <b><i>sometimes</i> </b>applies. I foresee an issue where a highly skilled 'normal' can actually outfight a reasonably competent Aberrant starting level character. (I suspect some people would be perfectly fine with that, but in a super-hero system Batman still has 'super-skills' essentially.)<br /> <br /> But going Dice Pool vs. Dice Pool, there's nothing showing you can do better as is, you just succeed regularly more often. And I only saw a difference in target number based on scale. So you can run into situation where Gina Mortal rolls really well because she has more dice, but the supposedly fairly epic superhero who can juggle knives and pick up cars has a much smaller dice pool and only rolls more average and can't hit her.<br /> <br /> Derived Values even makes that worse, because I can't see ever having Tier bonuses to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}